MATHEMATICS AS AN LMNO SYSTEM

A Meta-Structural Reconciliation of Mathematical Philosophy

Author: Kok Pian Gew (derived)
Status: Concept Paper v0.1
Date: 2026

⸻

ABSTRACT

Mathematics has historically been interpreted through competing philosophical frameworks, including Logicism, Formalism, Intuitionism, and Platonism. These schools are often treated as mutually exclusive explanations of the nature of mathematics.

This paper proposes that such divergence arises from pillar dominance within a unified system. Using the LMNO framework—Structure (L), Interpretation (M), Regime (N), and Realisation (O)—we show that each philosophical school isolates and elevates one component of a larger, irreducible system.

Mathematics is therefore not reducible to any single philosophical position. Instead, it is a multi-layered system in which structure, meaning, rules, and execution co-operate to produce stable, transmissible, and extensible knowledge.

