9. CONCLUSION

Mathematics is not:
	•	purely logical
	•	purely symbolic
	•	purely mental
	•	purely discovered

It is:

a structured system in which form, meaning, rule, and execution co-operate

Philosophical schools reflect partial views of this system.

The LMNO framework restores completeness.

